# Gitleaks allowlist - one fingerprint per line.
#
# Fingerprints are <commit>:<path>:<rule>:<line>, so each entry pins a single
# known finding in a single historical commit. A new leak, or the same string
# reintroduced in a new commit, still fails the scan.
#
# Both entries below are in commit cb7c57f9, the original flat project that was
# removed when this repository was rebuilt as a modular monorepo. Neither file
# exists on master any more, and neither value was ever a live credential - the
# legacy stack was never deployed.
#
# History is deliberately not rewritten for these: both are placeholders, and a
# force-push over a public default branch is a worse trade than two pinned
# exceptions. Anything that is a real secret must be rotated and purged
# instead - see SECURITY.md.

# optional-features.tf:83 - grafana.adminPassword = "admin123", a placeholder
# carrying its own "# Change in production" comment, in a chart release that
# was never applied. The current stack has no Grafana and sets no passwords in
# Terraform at all.
